// Central Kurdish (Sorani, ckb) translation rules
// Sorani uses a modified Perso-Arabic script (33 letters) written
// right-to-left. Unlike Arabic/Persian it is almost a true alphabet:
// vowels are written, except short /I/ which is unwritten between
// consonants. Words listed in ckb_list spell it out; otherwise a
// word-initial consonant cluster gets it (نڤێژ nIveZ, کتێب kIteb), or
// the first consonant is swallowed. Consonant + و/ی onsets (خوا xwa)
// are real clusters and are left alone.
// This file is UTF-8 encoded.

